WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.460
The Federal Trade Commission's Safeguards Rule implements part of the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act for financial institutions within the Commission's jurisdiction.

2
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.280
Coverage is based on activities, not on whether an organization calls itself a bank.

3
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:23.100
An institution may be covered when it is significantly engaged in an activity that is financial in nature or incidental to financial activity.

4
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.440
Current rule text controls; official examples inform but do not exhaust the analysis.

5
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:42.520
The protected subject is customer information: records containing nonpublic personal information about a customer of a financial institution, handled or maintained by or on behalf of the institution or its affiliates.

6
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.100
The definition reaches paper, electronic, and other forms.

7
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:55.360
It can include information about the institution's own customers and information supplied by another financial institution about that institution's customers.

8
00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:02.340
Customer status depends on the relevant financial relationship, so scope requires a data-and-relationship analysis.

9
00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:08.940
The Rule also reaches information systems that contain customer information or connect to systems that contain it.

10
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:16.720
Database-only inventories can miss endpoints, identities, networks, physical records, and supporting technology.

11
00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:31.860
The required program has three objectives: preserve security and confidentiality, protect against anticipated threats or hazards, and protect against unauthorized access or use that could cause substantial harm or inconvenience.

12
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.980
The Safeguards Rule concerns protection of customer information.

13
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:42.240
The separate Federal Trade Commission Privacy Rule addresses notice, sharing practices, and certain opt-out rights.

14
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:49.060
Other federal regulators, state laws, contracts, and sector obligations may apply independently.

15
00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:54.920
This course provides general education, not legal advice or a certification of compliance.

16
00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:03.100
When jurisdiction, customer status, or data scope is uncertain, the defensible next step is documented analysis with qualified legal and compliance review.
